xgis 1

/* §5 background-pattern consumption-side verification (#777 I-E): the pattern
 * rides the synthetic earth-surface show through the STANDARD fill-pattern
 * path — the show carries fillPattern, render-loop _resolveFillPatterns fills
 * the atlas UV + world repeat, and VTR routes it to fillPipelinePatternGround.
 * Tiling is WORLD-ANCHORED (Mercator metres — the pattern scrolls with the
 * map, MapLibre background-pattern semantics) across the whole world band; the
 * authored fill stays the band colour under/outside the pattern.
 *
 * A background-pattern-only style (no labels / icons / fill-patterns) still
 * loads its sprite atlas: ensureBackgroundPatternAtlas (label-pass.ts) fires
 * on `_backgroundPattern`, and its onLanded invalidate() re-arms the idle loop
 * so the pattern paints when the async atlas lands.
 *
 * Load with: /demo.html?id=fixture_bg_pattern&e2e=1&sprite=/fixture-sprite
 * §5 probe (orchestrator-run): the `pat` sprite is 128 red + 128 blue texels —
 * verification = red/blue pattern pixels present across the band at the
 * default camera; MapLibre A/B on the same style.
 */
background { fill: #1a1a2e pattern: pat }
